{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the men are shepherds of sheep, for they were men of livestock.</b> He told them that they are shepherds, but not that they graze animals belonging to others, for even with their own animals they have slaves and household members who graze them. Rather, their wealth was in livestock. And this is the meaning of \"for they were men of livestock\" — they had very great wealth and much labor in the abundant livestock that was theirs, for he did not wish to mention it except for the sake of honor."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:45:42.427604301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}